    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0021" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3A/611: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-29">January 29,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received January 29—12:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. For Knapp<anchor n="25" xml:id="d9-f1"/> from Spaeth. Yesterday Committee
                    sent cable to Argentina expressing satisfaction decision to break,<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d9-f2"/> noting decision <pb facs="0022" n="8" xml:id="pg8"/> was
                    taken because proof espionage activities undermining national sovereignty and
                    continental security and expressing Committee’s desire collaborate with
                    Argentina in study measures common defense Continent against Axis political
                    aggression. [Spaeth.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d9-f1" n="25" xml:id="d9-f1-content">
                <p>Laurence A. Knapp, Liaison Officer between the United States and the Committee,
                    and Special Assistant to the Attorney General of the United States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d9-f2" n="26" xml:id="d9-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence indicating United States interest in the break of diplomatic
                    relations between Argentina and the Axis, see <ref target="#pg228">pp. 228</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
